# The qwin instrument plus the pass-phase itemisation: every microsecond of a
# keyboard pass charged to one of twelve named segments, printed as `ph=`/`us=`
# on the qwin line. It is a rung and not a profile in its own right -- the
# twelve counter reads per pass cost scan rate, so a figure from this image is
# never a comparison point, and the difference against a plain `qwin` window of
# the same length in the same sitting is what prices the instrument itself.
# Outside the default sweep. Retired when the pass has an owner for every
# segment it splits.
ERA_SPLIT_QWIN_COUNT_ONLY_ENABLE := yes
ERA_PASS_PHASE_DIAGNOSTICS_ENABLE := yes
